# Blockingmachine element harvest — the real capture the live scan recorded.
#
# The real capture the live scan recorded, transcribed: the original recv-0*.json files lived in a
# scratch directory that was deliberately never committed, so these are the same elements as they
# were on the page, with the verdict the shipping model gave them BEFORE the five fixes that scan
# produced. Replaying them is how the harvest pipeline is tested against data nobody wrote for it:
# all six shapes were false positives, and four of them were hidden outright.
# Class and action are the report's own words. Confidence is stated only for the 33 spurious hides
# (98%); elsewhere it is the tier value the reported evidence implies. No candidate is ever labelled
# from it — these six are labelled by the person who reviewed them and called each one content.
# Sightings are capped at three per shape where the report counted more (MDN saw 5 scripts, the
# Guardian 8 scripts and 3 photos, GitHub 5 scripts and 7 footer links); the count that matters to
# the report is in the sightings field either way.
#
# The last five records are the other half of that day: the shapes the reviewer looked at and
# deliberately left alone. They are here because a queue that only ever holds defects is a queue
# that cannot tell a reviewer what to keep. Two of them are shapes the model already leaves alone
# and would never be harvested on its own, and one is a real detection the reviewer agreed with, so
# it carries the only 'hide' label in this file.
#
# Format: one element per line. The extension writes this shape on export, the hub reads it,
# and scripts/harvest-element-candidates.mjs --in turns it into the corpus candidate queue.
#
# Class and action are the live-scan report's own words. Confidence is stated only for the 33
# spurious hides (98%); elsewhere it is the tier value the reported evidence implies. No candidate is
# ever labelled from it — these are labelled by the person who reviewed them and called each one
# content, or, for the last record, agreed it should be removed.
